{"name":"Light Shell Haven","hex":"#f1e8ce","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"shell","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard external covering of an animal.\nThe calcareous or chitinous external covering of mollusks, crustaceans, and some other invertebrates.","The calcareous or chitinous external covering of mollusks, crustaceans, and some other invertebrates."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To remove the outer covering or shell of something.","To bombard, to fire projectiles at, especially with artillery."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shell"},{"term":"haven","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A harbour or anchorage protected from the sea.","A safe place."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put into, or provide with a haven."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haven"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shell Haven","blocks":[{"text":"Shell Haven was a port on the north bank of the Thames Estuary at the eastern end of Thurrock, Essex, England, and then an oil refinery. The refinery closed in 1999 and the site was purchased by DP World, who received planning consent in May 2007 for the new London Gateway deep-water container port at the site. The neighbouring Coryton Refinery remained in operation until 2012."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Shell_haven_191007.jpg/330px-Shell_haven_191007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shell_Haven"